<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Miss Anthony returns for her subsequent annual wellness visit, three weeks after her six-month heart failure review. She completed the health risk assessment before the visit. Her August bronchitis cleared within two weeks without antibiotics. Since her last wellness visit she has had no falls, emergency visits, or hospital stays. She reports good adherence, uses a weekly pill organizer, and has added no over-the-counter medicines. She is back to a full lecture and travel schedule and walks two miles most days. Her one new concern is difficulty following questions from the back of crowded halls, more on the right. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Subsequent annual wellness visit</td></tr><tr><td>New concern</td><td>Trouble hearing in crowded halls, worse on the right</td></tr><tr><td>Safety events</td><td>No falls, emergency visits, or hospital stays in the past year</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Adherent with a weekly pill organizer; no new over-the-counter medicines or supplements</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Heart failure with preserved ejection fraction and hypertensive heart disease, both controlled</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent in all activities and instrumental activities of daily living</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, and better than in the spring</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Lives with her sister; close circle of colleagues; no loneliness; stress from her work schedule is manageable</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>Never smoker; no alcohol; walks two miles most days; simple diet with moderate salt; sleeps about seven hours</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent in bathing, dressing, eating, toileting, and transfers</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Manages her own medicines, money, correspondence, and travel arrangements</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Smoke detectors working; handrails on both sides of the stairs; one loose hall rug</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Difficulty hearing in large rooms; reading glasses; last eye examination more than a year ago</td></tr><tr><td>Bladder</td><td>Urgency on the days she takes furosemide, without leakage</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>No concerns from her or her family</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

