<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed, personalized prevention plan updated, and a written copy given. Depression, alcohol, cognitive, and fall-risk screens are negative. [S]<list><item>Next annual wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Heart failure with preserved ejection fraction (I50.32)</content>. Compensated, with symptoms only on long stair climbs. The KCCQ-12 score rose from 52 at diagnosis to 76 in September, and her weight is stable. [S]<list><item>Continue empagliflozin, spironolactone, and as-needed furosemide by the weight plan.</item><item>Basic metabolic panel and magnesium with the next heart failure review in about three months, then every three to six months on the CMID schedule.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypertensive heart disease (I11.0)</content>. Blood pressure 124/72 mmHg, below the 130/80 target, without orthostatic symptoms. [S]<list><item>No change.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Reduced hearing, right ear</content>. New concern, confirmed by a failed whispered-voice test on the right. Hearing loss is common at her age and treatable, and it matters for her public speaking. [S]<list><item>Refer to audiology for a formal hearing evaluation.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Urinary urgency on furosemide days</content>. Expected effect of the diuretic, without incontinence or infection symptoms. [S]<list><item>Take as-needed furosemide in the morning and plan it around lectures and travel.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Fall risk</content>. Low, with no falls in the past year and a Timed Up and Go of 9 seconds. [S]<list><item>Secure or remove the loose hall rug.</item><item>Continue daily walking.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>High-dose vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended at her age; she plans to get it at her pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PCV20 given in March; no further doses needed</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Single dose given in March</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two-dose series completed four years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap six years ago; next dose due in four years</td></tr><tr><td>Bone density (DXA)</td><td>Ordered</td><td>No prior scan on record; recommended for women 65 and older, and her low body weight raises fracture risk</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol misuse screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mini-Cog 5 of 5</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Timed Up and Go 9 seconds; home-safety advice given</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>Referred</td><td>Audiology referral for a failed right whispered-voice test</td></tr><tr><td>Eye examination</td><td>Due</td><td>More than a year since her last examination; she will book with her optometrist</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>LDL cholesterol 96 mg/dL and HbA1c 5.5% in March</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Age 85; after discussion she declines further screening</td></tr><tr><td>Breast cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Evidence is insufficient after 75; after discussion she declines further mammograms</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not recommended after 65 with adequate prior screening</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoker</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: High-dose influenza vaccine, 1905-1906 season [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, heart failure monograph (2026); Medicare Wellness Visits (Medicare Learning Network) (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Audiology referral and DXA scan ordered. Heart failure review with laboratory tests in about three months. Next annual wellness visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
